  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{4}{3s+6}.$",
  "worked_solution": "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+2}=\\frac{4}{3s+6},\\,s>-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}} & =\\frac{4}{3s+6} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{3s+6}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{3s+6}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{3s+6}} & =\\frac{4}{3}{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
